This is a YAML configuration file for a computational model titled *"sensitivity_trust_decay.yml"*, part of the repository [prometheusWaluigi/piston-leak-lab](https://github.com/prometheusWaluigi/piston-leak-lab). The file defines parameters for a simulation combining ordinary differential equations (ODE) and agent-based modeling (ABM) to study the dynamics of *"trust decay"* in the context of a hypothetical *"piston-leak"* scenario, likely involving information dissemination or crisis management. The model appears to explore how trust interacts with entropy, suppression, and exogenous shocks, potentially in a context of public health, security, or social systems under stress.

**Genre and Subject:**  
The source belongs to the genre of computational modeling and simulation configuration files. Its apparent subject is the analysis of trust decay and entropy dynamics in a system where suppression mechanisms and exogenous leaks influence the behavior of agents and overall system stability. It seems to be part of an experimental or research project, possibly related to crisis simulation, misinformation, or organizational resilience.

**Main Ideas:**  
The simulation explores the sensitivity of trust decay to various parameters, such as the suppression penalty on trust (`gamma1`) and entropy gain from suppression (`alpha2`). The model includes a Monte-Carlo ensemble with a random seed and parameter sweeps, specifically over `alpha1`, which governs trust decay relative to entropy. The system also incorporates a Watts-Strogatz network of 3,000 agents, weighted influence fields (believers, skeptics, agnostics), and a noise model with exogenous leak shocks. The simulation runs for one "pandemic year" (`t_max: 365`), and outputs include parameter heatmaps and plots, with results saved to a directory.

